{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1032472-spirit-familiar-help","id":1032472,"title":"Spirit Familiar Help","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-01-15T21:09:08-08:00","id":1032472,"title":"Spirit Familiar Help","content":"I have a Thyrsus player that freed a bear spirit during his Awakening which became his Familiar. Can anyone out there help me define it&quot;s influence, ban &amp; bane? The Spirit is Rank 2.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1470,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","user":"Johnny Awesome","date":". 01-16-2017, 12:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-15T22:36:10-08:00","id":1032488,"title":"","content":"Traditionally its Influence at that Rank would be 'bear.' I can understand that that might not seem fun but it could probably grow later. And obviously you could justify something else depending on the bear. Sometimes bears symbolize courage or strength. For some reason I think guardianship. What was the bear spirit doing when you encountered it? These could also help signify its tell.<br /> <br /> And of course I'm going with 'standard' bears, for all I know it's a polar or panda bear.<br /> <br /> As it happens, there's a sample bear spirit in Predators, also Rank 2. Here's part of it.<br /> <br /> 'While they may appear placid until disturbed, it\u2019s a deceptive fa\u00e7ade. Within the blink of an eye, bear-spirits manifest their true capacity for fury and ferocity. They are extremely strong and determined, if not overly quick-witted. While they are capable of feats of remarkable intelligence, for the most part, they tend to be very goal-oriented. They move with a lumbering gait unless prodded to action, when their true grace and swiftness becomes belatedly apparent. They are one of the more aggressively cannibalistic types of animal-spirit, quick to turn on the smaller and weaker members of their \u201cspecies.\u201d'<br /> <br /> For a Ban it says this, 'Some bear-spirits are associated with guardianship (knew it), and may be held under bans that do not allow them to initiate an attack unless otherwise provoked, or restrict their movement to certain territories. Others have seasonal bans, losing much of their strength in winter or summer (depending on the spirit in question).'<br /> <br /> You said it was 'freed.' If it real world bear was in captivity, it might have a ban or bane based on the methods used to contain it, such as it can't leave a closed room by itself, or it could have a bane of electricity, representing stun batons used to torment it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T03:43:03-08:00","id":1032574,"title":"","content":"For Ridden of this Bear spirit, here you go inspiration. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://i.imgur.com/aeQUxBt.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T05:42:35-08:00","id":1032602,"title":"","content":"The bear was trapped by tass from a hallow in the form of bind weed if that helps with anything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T05:56:39-08:00","id":1032607,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1032472-spirit-familiar-help?p=1032488#post1032488\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Traditionally its Influence at that Rank would be 'bear.' I can understand that that might not seem fun but it could probably grow later.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you are talking about growing in Rank (you might no! My Spirit Fu is not very good), problem here is that you can't have a Familiar above Rank 2, as ascending ot a Rank 3 - even temporarily through use of Dot 3 boosting spells - instantly breaks the Familiar bond.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T06:00:59-08:00","id":1032608,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1032472-spirit-familiar-help?p=1032607#post1032607\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you are talking about growing in Rank (you might no! My Spirit Fu is not very good), problem here is that you can't have a Familiar above Rank 2, as ascending ot a Rank 3 - <b>even temporarily through use of Dot 3 boosting spells </b>- instantly breaks the Familiar bond.</div> </div> </div> </div>Where's this bolded part mentioned? That seems...dumb, honestly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T08:27:37-08:00","id":1032682,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1032472-spirit-familiar-help?p=1032608#post1032608\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where's this bolded part mentioned? That seems...dumb, honestly.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/635185-ghost-familliars-which-ranks?p=635614#post635614\">There's a little bit here</a>. It just seems to suggest that there's another ability required for higher Ranked beings. Right now it's represented by the Familiar Merit being specifically for Rank 1 and 2 entities, and there just not being one for Rank 3. The link probably gets too strong. It's one thing sharing your soul with a lesser creature but Rank 3's are geists and people, it would probably fuck up the mage and familiar without some special barrier in place.<br /> <br /> However, that said, though there's no Experience chart, a spirit can still grow and develop and form a new Influence without going up in Rank.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 01-16-2017, 11:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T08:56:08-08:00","id":1032692,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1032472-spirit-familiar-help?p=1032608#post1032608\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where's this bolded part mentioned? That seems...dumb, honestly.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;The spirit may not be greater than Rank 2.&quot;<br /> <br /> Spells stop working on a target once it ceases to be a viable subject for them \u2014 and a Familiar that reaches the level of spiritual nobility has stopped being a Rank 2 spirit just as surely as a character who ends a curse lowering their Resolve to 1 has stopped being vulnerable to the Potency 2 Amorality spell that was exploiting it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T12:10:02-08:00","id":1032814,"title":"","content":"Time for a me to throw down some house rules, I guess.<br /> I'll have to include not canceling spells that take advantage of a temporary vulnerability once it expires, too. <br /> <br /> I find subjects being able to suddenly Withstand effects that have already been active on them previously because they got a temporary boost in abilities to be absurd. Withstanding effects like that is only mentioned to be factored in when the spell is cast, there's no implication that it should continue afterwards. That makes cancelling active effects with a single turn of WP expenditure far too easy.<br /> <br /> Note that I'm not saying you're wrong, it's just <i>really</i> not for me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3570,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","user":"lnodiv","date":". 01-16-2017, 03:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T12:28:46-08:00","id":1032835,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1032472-spirit-familiar-help?p=1032682#post1032682\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/635185-ghost-familliars-which-ranks?p=635614#post635614\">There's a little bit here</a>. It just seems to suggest that there's another ability required for higher Ranked beings. Right now it's represented by the Familiar Merit being specifically for Rank 1 and 2 entities, and there just not being one for Rank 3. The link probably gets too strong. It's one thing sharing your soul with a lesser creature but Rank 3's are geists and people, it would probably fuck up the mage and familiar without some special barrier in place.</div> </div> </div> </div>And this is why I prepered homebrew Advanced Familar Merit as there is obvoius hole in 2E <b>Mage</b> system on this front. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ( And added Ghost Mage option for Ghost Familiar. )<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/917247-2e-optional-advanced-mage-merits#post917247\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Familiar, Advanced (\u2022\u2022\u2022) </b>by me<br /> <b>Prerequisites: Familiar \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022</b><br /> <b>Effect:</b> Your character has been bonded with very potent Familiar ( see <b>MtAw</b> 2E p. 101) in exchange for it\u2019s safety from bleeding Essence. This Merit indicate a Rank 3 entity.<br /> <b>Drawback:</b> This Familiar is more powerful than normal of his lower kin \u2013 he start to makes demands. Once per story he can ask you to perform minor favor. If character miss three of them in row, Familiar will broke the bond and look for other means to survive in Fallen World. If he leaves you, Sanctity of Merits rule is still viable.<br /> <br /> <b>Familiar, Epic (\u2022\u2022\u2022 ) by\u200b me</b><br /> <b>Prerequisites: </b>Advanced Familiar \u2022\u2022\u2022<br /> <b>Effect: </b>Your character has been bonded with the most potent Familiar ( see MtAw 2E p. 101) in exchange for it\u2019s safety from bleeding Essence. This Merit indicate a Rank 4 entity that is agreeing to terms of partnership with character.<br /> <b>Drawback: </b>This Familiar is most powerful of his kind \u2013 and he makes demands. Once per chapter he can ask you to perform large favor. If character miss three of them in row, Familiar will broke the bond and look for other means to survive in Fallen World. If he leaves you, Sanctity of Merits rule is still viable.<br /> <br /> <b>Ghost Mage Familiar</b> <b>( \u2022 ) </b>by\u200b me<br /> <b>Prerequisites: Ghost Familiar \u2022\u2022+</b><br /> <b>Effect:</b> Your character has been bonded with a Ghost Familiar that was a fellow mage in life. This means that the Numina which the familiar has may be pulled from Awakened spells, rather than from the normal numina list \u2013 or Influences based on Arcana. These represent spells that the familiar had as Praxes during life. Even if living Awakened could have much larger repertoire of spells or powers, his ghost can \u2018remember\u2019 only as much as his Rank let him to have. Besides this exceptions, a Ghost Mage follows all the same rules as any other Familiar, and are treated as a Rank based on the <i>Familiar</i> Merit.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 01-16-2017, 03:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T20:32:29-08:00","id":1033119,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1032472-spirit-familiar-help?p=1032814#post1032814\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I find subjects being able to suddenly Withstand effects that have already been active on them previously because they got a temporary boost in abilities to be absurd. Withstanding effects like that is only mentioned to be factored in when the spell is cast, there's no implication that it should continue afterwards.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>The spell specifically is still active and counts against spell control regardless of its ineffectiveness if Withstand reduces its Potency to zero</i>. I gave an example of a conditionally-vulnerable target losing their conditional vulnerability because it makes the point better than the reverse, not because any negation ends the spell completely.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That makes cancelling active effects with a single turn of WP expenditure far too easy. </div> </div> </div>&quot;One Willpower buys you one turn of extra resistance to the spell affecting you&quot; is not &quot;One turn of Willpower completely negates a spell.&quot; The Familiar Manifestation can only be granted through a spell that only works on willing ephemeral beings of low Rank \u2014 regardless of whether the spell <i>breaks</i> if you bolster your Knight into a Baron, it's not going to provide its benefit to something that's outgrown the easy definition of &quot;animistic reflection&quot;/&quot;psychic archetype&quot;/&quot;remnant of the deceased.&quot;<br /> <br /> This is a spell that only becomes available at the level where the default Arcanum grants you innate status among the spirit-courts and the ability to scour away the existence of any viable target for the spell \u2014 it's generally not the purpose of a Familiar to serve as a way around the limits of Reach in dealing aggravated damage to one of the most durable/resilient macrocategories of character/phenomenon in the setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T23:35:15-08:00","id":1033184,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1032472-spirit-familiar-help?p=1033119#post1033119\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>The spell specifically is still active and counts against spell control regardless of its ineffectiveness if Withstand reduces its Potency to zero</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good point there, I'd overlooked that. <br /> So it would just be one turn of resistance, which makes much more sense.<br /> <br /> I don't mind Familiar temporarily not providing its benefits if the subject temporarily increases in Rank. The part that bothers me is that the implication in Dave's post is that the spell fails entirely. If you're temporarily an invalid subject, imo you should only temporarily be unaffected by the spell at worst.<br /> <br /> The way the Withstand issue actually works kind of just strengthens that opinion for me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-21T07:22:30-08:00","id":1035704,"title":"","content":"What would you think the game effects of Influence: Guardianship 2 would be?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-21T10:11:24-08:00","id":1035737,"title":"","content":"It would probably be Guardian or Protection. Strengthen could give a bonus to rolls taking place while guarding someone or something else, perhaps give them some Defense bonus. Control or Manipulation might make someone more inclined to or automatically protect something. Create could create armor or a bear.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-21T12:13:47-08:00","id":1035781,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1032472-spirit-familiar-help?p=1035737#post1035737\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It would probably be Guardian or Protection. Strengthen could give a bonus to rolls taking place while guarding someone or something else, perhaps give them some Defense bonus. Control or Manipulation might make someone more inclined to or automatically protect something. Create could create armor or a bear.</div> </div> </div> </div>A... guard bear?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-21T12:18:58-08:00","id":1035783,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1032472-spirit-familiar-help?p=1035781#post1035781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A... guard bear?</div> </div> </div> </div>I was working off the assumption that Johnny was still talking about the bear spirit from their first post. A bear spirit of protection wouldn't create a human security guard.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-21T13:19:20-08:00","id":1035808,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1032472-spirit-familiar-help?p=1035783#post1035783\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I was working off the assumption that Johnny was still talking about the bear spirit from their first post. A bear spirit of protection wouldn't create a human security guard.</div> </div> </div> </div>I rather like the mental image of a spirit bear dressed up as a security guard.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"use